{0 Affect {%html: <span class="version">%%VERSION%%</span>%}}

Affect is a streamlined and natural concurrency model for OCaml.

It provides parallel asynchronous functions and first-class synchronous
actions to orchestrate them. The resulting
{{!page-concurrency_model}concurrency model} has structured cooperative
concurrency, structured cancellation and structured effect handling.

{b Warning.} These APIs are still subject to change in the future,
especially the private ones. Feedback and suggestions are welcome on
the project's issue tracker.

{1:manuals Manuals}

The following manuals are available:

{ul
{- The {{!quick_start}quick start} should do so.}
{- The short {{!page-concurrency_model}concurrency model} is
   recommended reading to form your mental model.}
{- The {{!Affect.Action.basics}basics of actions} should be read if
   you have advanced synchronization needs.}
{- The {{!page-cookbook}cookbook} has a few conventions, recipes
   and answers to common questions.}
{- The {{!page-design}design notes} explains a few design choices made by the
   library.}}

{1:library_affect Library [affect]}

{2:asynchronous_funs Asynchronous functions}

Asynchronous functions are made available in an extended {!Stdlib.Fun}
module.

{!modules:
Affect
Affect.Fun.Async
}

{2:actions Actions}

The {{!Affect.Action}[Action]} module provides first-class
synchronization ({{!page-cookbook.actions_own_handling}can
be} used independently). A few derived synchronization structures are
provided.

{!modules:
Affect.Action
Affect.Port
Affect.Cell.Drop
Affect.Cell.Lazy
Affect.Cell.Once
Affect.Semaphore
}

{1:library_unix Library [affect.unix]}

{!modules:
Affect_unix
Affect_unix.Unix
Affect_unix.Mtime
Affect_unix.Ptime
}

{1:library_cli Library [affect.cli]}

{!modules:
Affect_cli
}

{1:library_tmp Library [affect.tmp]}

This library has unstable functionality that will be moved to another
library in the future. It may still be useful if you are playing with
affect.

{!modules:
Net
}

{1:quick_start Quick start}

{[
open Affect

let main () =
  Fun.Async.main @@ fun () ->
  let f0 = Fun.Async.call (fun () -> 1) in
  let f1 = Fun.Async.call (fun () -> 2) in
  print_int (Fun.Async.get f0 + Fun.Async.get f1);
  0

let () = if !Sys.interactive then () else exit (main ())
]}

See other blueprints in the {{!page-cookbook.blueprints}cookbook}.
